1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,040
Introducing NAADI.

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:07,440
Your loom has been telling you for weeks.

3
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:13,110
NAADI learns each machine's own normal, without a single fault label.

4
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:19,920
Every six hours, it punches a card. By card 24, it had caught the change, before anyone heard a thing.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,920
Type the bearing number from the motor plate, and the physics does the rest.

6
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,090
The envelope hears it: peaks right on the outer-race frequency.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,740
Outer-race defect: 88.6%.

8
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:34,590
Same bearing. Two bills.

9
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:43,240
6.5 days are left. A breakdown costs over ₹21,000. Thursday's power cut? Just ₹1,280.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,310
The agents prepare. You decide.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,740
They line up the part and the technician, and every number comes from a tested tool.

12
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:55,070
One tap, and the drafts go to your phone.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,410
In simulation: 17.8 days of warning (median).

14
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:01,090
For every loom, chakki and pump set.

15
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,850
Offline. In English, Hindi and Marathi.

16
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:07,080
NAADI. Machine pulse intelligence for small factories.
